{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3418","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3418","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3418\",\"parent_revision\":\"9f562574edda3cca42e5d0b6c8f518cf243a27ad0b4d839149a9a063ec42f3ad\",\"root_revision\":\"9f562574edda3cca42e5d0b6c8f518cf243a27ad0b4d839149a9a063ec42f3ad\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-09-04\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n`FileCache._work_item_snapshots()` logs and silently drops any corrupt/unreadable local snapshot (0-byte body, bad UTF-8, escaping symlink, etc. \u2014 this is the salvage policy PR #3405 fixed and hardened). That drop makes the item indistinguishable, downstream, from one that was never cached at all.\\n\\nUnder `ReconcileScope.INCREMENTAL` (`backend/github_work_items.py:564`, `reconciliation.py:281`), the remote item is only re-fetched if it appears in the incremental diff since the last watermark. If the corrupted item hasn't changed remotely, it's absent from that diff too \u2014 `_plan_item(None, ...)` is never invoked for it, and `backlog_list`/`load_records()` omits it entirely, presenting it as if it doesn't exist. This directly contradicts the stated invariant in `plugins/development-harness/AGENTS.md:87`: \\\"Cache misses are unavailable data, not authoritative empty results.\\\" The item stays permanently missing until either the remote item changes again (triggering re-fetch) or a full `ReconcileScope.INITIAL` resync runs.\\n\\nThis is a pre-existing gap in the corrupt-snapshot salvage design itself (the \\\"one bad file must not crash the batch\\\" pattern, mirroring `_CacheStateStore._salvage_field`) \u2014 not introduced by PR #3405's fixes, which only closed loopholes that let corruption crash the *entire* enumeration instead of just dropping the one bad entry. Fixing the incremental-reconcile blind spot means touching `github_work_items.py`'s and `reconciliation.py`'s scope-diffing logic, well beyond PR #3405's stated purpose (a crash fix). Related to #3412 (no skip-count surfaced to callers) but more severe: this is not just missing observability, it's data presented as absent when it may actually exist remotely.\\n\\nUser-provided context: candidate fixes include forcing a full resync when any snapshot is dropped, or making the INCREMENTAL diff explicitly check \\\"known local keys with no snapshot\\\" against the remote list rather than only diffing by watermark. Exact design is grooming/architecture work.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Code review on PR #3405 (cache-crash fix)\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-09-04\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"e1986b84c81ae8201e46745e517ccb35cf62b6324502b0141ce94ed80d1e885e\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABStom-g\"}"}